---
title: "Password Input"
description: "Password field with a button that shows or hides the value."
tags: [forms, accessibility, javascript]
usage: |
  Wrap the label, the `<input type="password">` and a `<button type="button">` in
  an element with the `password-input` class. Then call `initPasswordInputs()`:

  ```js
  import { initPasswordInputs } from "./password-input.js";

  initPasswordInputs(); // or initPasswordInputs(root, ".password-input")
  ```
accessibility: |
  - The button text switches between "Show password" and "Hide password", so it
    always describes the action it performs.
  - `aria-controls` on the button points at the input it changes.
  - Keep `autocomplete` (`current-password` or `new-password`) so password
    managers work.
customProperties:
  "--password-input-gap": "Space between the input and the button."
  "--password-input-label-gap": "Space between the label and the field."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<div class="password-input">
  <label for="password">Password</label>
  <div>
    <input id="password" type="password" name="password" autocomplete="current-password">
    <button type="button" aria-controls="password">Show password</button>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="module">
  import { initPasswordInputs } from "./password-input.js";

  initPasswordInputs();
</script>
